1
00:00:02,736 --> 00:00:03,970
Hello, my name is William Coe,

2
00:00:04,037 --> 00:00:06,940
and I'm going to show you how to tie the scrunchie or wedding cravat.

3
00:00:07,341 --> 00:00:11,211
First off, do up your top button on your wing-collar shirt.

4
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,710
It could be a standard wing or a deep wing, depending on how you want to wear it.

5
00:00:16,152 --> 00:00:21,288
It goes round the collar and roughly where one of the blades comes up.

6
00:00:22,015 --> 00:00:24,925
In fact, that should be leveled with one of the... your top button.

7
00:00:25,362 --> 00:00:26,727
And it's very straightforward.

8
00:00:26,793 --> 00:00:29,363
You take one end over the other,

9
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:31,565
round the back,

10
00:00:32,732 --> 00:00:33,634
round the front,

11
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:37,040
come up from the back,

12
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:39,907
pull all the way through.

13
00:00:40,307 --> 00:00:44,044
Try not to pull the knot too tight, because you want a nice big ruffled knot.

14
00:00:44,778 --> 00:00:48,015
You take the shorter blade, push it through the front,

15
00:00:48,944 --> 00:00:54,454
pull down, and then just pull up, cover your top button.

16
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:59,893
You might need to look in the mirror, at this point, or get someone to help you.

17
00:00:59,958 --> 00:01:02,963
And don't worry about the blade lengths because they will be tucked

18
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:05,299
under the waistcoat that will come up at least to here.

19
00:01:05,767 --> 00:01:07,434
All we're interested in doing

20
00:01:07,501 --> 00:01:13,607
is making sure we've got a nice, rich, large knot that covers your top button

21
00:01:13,674 --> 00:01:15,842
and makes the whole scrunch look attractive.

22
00:01:17,246 --> 00:01:18,445
And there we go.
